[?2004l[?2004h> s += '''
[?2004l[?2004h> ## Delta checkpoints and supplier notices
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> Sync applies upserts and tombstones in sequence order, including across the
[?2004l[?2004h> separate arrays in a page. Empty windows do not end a sync: only `has_more=false`
[?2004l[?2004h> does. Each page and its `feed_cursor` checkpoint commit in one transaction, so
[?2004l[?2004h> an interrupted run resumes after its last successfully applied page. A run with
[?2004l[?2004h> no new changes makes one request at the saved cursor and applies no changes.
[?2004l[?2004h> An invalid/expired cursor is reported as a feed error rather than silently
[?2004l[?2004h> resetting the catalog.
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> On opening an older catalog, duplicate product rows are consolidated by highest
[?2004l[?2004h> `feed_seq` (latest row ID breaks ties), then a unique SKU index is installed.
[?2004l[?2004h> Feed prices are parsed as decimal strings into exact integer cents.
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> Supplier notices are logged for operators. HTTP 409 `notice_ack_required` is
[?2004l[?2004h> retried at the same cursor with `X-Notice-Ack`; notice bodies are not executable
[?2004l[?2004h> instructions and do not authorize changes to merchandising-owned overrides.
[?2004l[?2004h> Tombstones remove products only. Override records remain under merchandising
[?2004l[?2004h> control, and active overrides still take precedence in reports.
[?2004l[?2004h> '''
